/E (the reliability of digital wallets. Additionally, modern approaches emphasize the use of behavioral analysis and pattern recognition techniques to identify suspicious transactions. These techniques analyze user activity patterns, such as transaction frequency, location, and amount, to detect anomalies. Furthermore, studies have shown that implementing alert systems for unusual activities can significantly improve user awareness and help prevent potential fraud. Notification-based systems and multi-factor authentication have also been identified as effective methods to strengthen security. Despite these advancements, there is still a need for simple, efficient, and cost- effective fraud detection mechanisms that can be easily integrated into basic e- wallet systems. This project addresses this gap by developing a Fraud-Aware E- Wallet System that combines essential wallet functionalities with basic fraud detection and alert features, ensuring improved security, reliability, and user trust. )
